# ====================================================================================
# BooksTrack Backend - Environment Variables Template
# ====================================================================================
#
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Copy this file to .env (git-ignored)
# 2. Replace placeholder values with actual secrets
# 3. For production deployment, use: wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME
#
# Example:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   # Edit .env with your actual API keys
#   npx wrangler dev  # Local development uses .env automatically
#
# Production Deployment:
#   wrangler secret put GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY
#   (paste your actual key when prompted)
#
# ====================================================================================

# ====================================================================================
# External API Keys (Required for development)
# ====================================================================================
# Sprint 2 Thin Client: GOOGLE_BOOKS_API_KEY and ISBNDB_API_KEY no longer needed
# BooksTrack delegates all book enrichment to Alexandria (no direct external API calls)
#
# Only GEMINI_API_KEY is still required (for AI bookshelf scanning and CSV parsing)
# ====================================================================================

# AI API keys (for bookshelf scanning and CSV parsing)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ====================================================================================
# Alexandria Service Binding (Cloudflare Workers)
# ====================================================================================
# BooksTrack uses Alexandria service binding for book enrichment (configured in wrangler.jsonc)
# For external URL fallback (local dev without service binding):
#   ALEXANDRIA_BASE_URL=https://alexandria.ooheynerds.com
#
# For Cloudflare Access authentication (if Alexandria is behind Access):
#   wrangler secret put ALEXANDRIA_CLIENT_ID
#   wrangler secret put ALEXANDRIA_CLIENT_SECRET
# ====================================================================================

# ====================================================================================
# Wrangler System Variables (CI/CD and Production)
# ====================================================================================
# These variables control Wrangler CLI behavior during development and deployment.
# See: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/system-environment-variables/

# Authentication (Required for CI/CD)
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your_cloudflare_account_id_here
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your_cloudflare_api_token_here

# Logging Configuration (Optional)
# WRANGLER_LOG=debug                           # Log level: none, error, warn, info, debug
# WRANGLER_LOG_PATH=./logs/wrangler.log        # Path to log file (creates if not exists)

# Telemetry (Optional - disable for privacy/compliance)
# WRANGLER_SEND_METRICS=false                  # Disable anonymous usage metrics

# Output Formatting (Optional - useful for CI/CD)
# NO_COLOR=1                                   # Disable ANSI color codes
# FORCE_COLOR=0                                # Force disable colors (overrides NO_COLOR)

# ====================================================================================
# Environment-Specific Configuration (Advanced)
# ====================================================================================
# For multiple environments, create separate .env files:
#
# .env.production    - Production secrets (never commit!)
# .env.staging       - Staging environment (if using staging)
# .env.development   - Development overrides
#
# Load specific environment:
#   export $(cat .env.production | xargs) && wrangler deploy
#
# ====================================================================================

# ====================================================================================
# Security Best Practices
# ====================================================================================
# ✅ DO:
#   - Keep .env in .gitignore (NEVER commit secrets)
#   - Use wrangler secret put for production secrets
#   - Rotate API keys quarterly
#   - Use separate API keys for dev/staging/production
#
# ❌ DON'T:
#   - Commit .env or .env.production to version control
#   - Share API keys in Slack/email
#   - Use production keys in local development
#   - Log API keys in console.log or error messages
#
# ====================================================================================
